## 🚀 Deployment

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/<repository-name>.git
cd <repository-name>
```

### 2. Build the Docker image

```bash
docker build -t flask-app .
```

### 3. Run locally

```bash
docker run -p 5000:5000 flask-app
```

Open:

```text
http://localhost:5000
```

Health check:

```text
http://localhost:5000/health
```

---

## ⚙️ GitHub Actions

The workflow automates:

```text
Checkout
   ↓
AWS OIDC Authentication
   ↓
ECR Authentication
   ↓
Docker Build
   ↓
Docker Push
   ↓
ECS Deployment
```

A typical workflow file is:

```text
.github/workflows/deploy.yml
```

Secrets and credentials should not contain long-lived AWS access keys when OIDC is configured.

---

## 🔑 IAM Security

The GitHub Actions IAM role should follow the **principle of least privilege**.

Permissions should be limited to the AWS resources required by the deployment process, such as:

```text
ECR
 ├── Authenticate
 ├── Push Image
 └── Describe Repository

ECS
 ├── Register Task Definition
 ├── Update Service
 └── Describe Deployment
```

Avoid granting unnecessary:

```text
AdministratorAccess
```

to the GitHub Actions role.

